From 682fc6a02b3e3585738e870dcbbee7460adeceb9 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Hank Yeomans <hank@quorra.ah.local>
Date: Sat, 10 Oct 2026 14:36:47 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 50/61] sampler/scheduler: a NaN/Inf logits row aborts that
 request, not the server (recipe T3.13 / C10)

- Sampler.forward (outside the decode graph): under SGLANG_DSV41_REJECT_NAN_ROWS (default on)
  compute nan_rows = isnan|isposinf per row, then nan_to_num_ the logits (NaN -> -1e30,
  +inf -> 1e30, -inf kept so grammar masks survive). Well-formed rows are bit-identical.
- LogitsProcessorOutput.nan_rows; copy_to_cpu moves it D2H beside next_token_ids.
- batch_result_processor: before update_finish_state in the prefill (non-beam) and decode
  paths, a flagged row gets FINISH_ABORT(..., INTERNAL_SERVER_ERROR, "NonFiniteLogits") and an
  ERROR log line `[non-finite-logits] rid=... row=... mode=...`; the tokenizer manager turns it
  into an HTTP 500 JSON error for that request only. Off / spec / row-count mismatch -> no-op.
- kt_nan_inject.py: KT_NAN_INJECT="row=r,bs=b,step=n,layer=l" test hook (rank 0, fires once,
  armed by breakable_cuda_graph_backend.replay via KtRuntime.nan_inject, adds a NaN to one row of
  the MoE output after the CPU add). Diagnostic only; unset in production.

Verified on the recipe's instrumented serve (row=1,bs=4,step=3,layer=20): exactly one of four
concurrent requests returns 500 "non-finite logits ...", the other three run to max_tokens, the
next C4 group is 4 x 200, /health 200, same-prompt C4 consistency PASS.

Amp-Thread-ID: https://ampcode.com/threads/T-01a0c10b-a5f8-77fc-b238-7147d12ccf29
Co-authored-by: Amp <amp@ampcode.com>
